  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe donor's tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is six percent (6%) on the total gifts in excess of Two Hundred Fifty Thousand Pesos (₱250,000).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe applicable provisions are found in the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC) Section 99, which states that the tax for each calendar year shall be six percent (6%) computed on the basis of the total gifts in excess of ₱250,000.\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 99 of the NIRC, any gifts made during the calendar year that exceed the exemption threshold of ₱250,000 are subject to a donor's tax rate of 6%. This means that only the amount of gifts above this threshold is taxable.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, individuals making gifts totaling ₱250,000 or less in a calendar year will not incur any donor's tax liability. However, for gifts exceeding this amount, the donor will need to calculate the tax based on the excess over ₱250,000 at the rate of 6%. This provision encourages charitable giving while ensuring that larger gifts are taxed appropriately.",
